title The address read from the other end
prompt autonomous lap -- the DIFFUSER lane, picking up the falsifier the previous lap left named
rota lap 4199, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the concrete fact before the argument about it, which is the whole method of this lap: the tidy hypothesis was mine and the graph refused it
think The previous lap closed by naming its own next step exactly -- measure the free geometry at PARTIAL hole classes, since 800 members on an 840-vertex shape leaves 40 holes no whole class can hold. That is a research falsifier with a cheap experiment behind it, so the lap took it rather than opening anything new.
think The hypothesis was clean enough to be suspicious: the classes of an (n,k)-star nest, 840 splits 120, 20, 4, 1, so 40 holes are two whole classes of 20 and the greedy decomposition should cost what the whole class cost -- nothing. The elegant part was that the arrangement testing it is one line: sort addresses by their FAR END first and every nested class becomes a contiguous run, so the greedy answer is what a sequential allocator already produces, reading the address from the other end.
think The graph refused it. Forty-two whole level-2 classes, all 20 vertices, all leaving one component and an unmoved diameter, cost between 3 and 491 lost packets of 9,828. A 164-fold spread across sets that are identical in size and connectivity, which means the elder freedom belongs to the far-end class specifically and does not descend the ladder beneath it.
think Two findings survived and one is worth a builder's afternoon. The leftover addresses are nearly free -- 42 holes cost 457 where 40 cost 429, a rounding error rather than a cliff, which is the falsifier answered. And the same contiguous run either partitions the shape or does not, decided only by which end of the address is significant: 20 holes of S(6,3) door-major leave three components and 600 unreachable pairs, far-end-major leave one component.
obs The lap caught its own method breaking before it caught the finding. Scored the sibling scan's way -- targets sampled from each arrangement's own live set -- `class_partial` ranked BEST of five arrangements at three targets and WORST by a factor of fourteen at fifteen. So the scan samples targets from the whole address space and holds them fixed across arrangements, skips a target a hole set killed, and COUNTS it as `targets_dead=` rather than replacing it with a live one, which would have let the same drift back through a smaller door. The default target count is twelve, and it was chosen by measuring rather than by taste.
obs The sweep leg shipped its first draft with the exact fault the sibling paper is famous for catching. It routed from one target, and `block` at 20 holes read a clean zero-lost over 19 pairs while the shape stood in three components -- the target had been all but isolated, and a line saying nothing went wrong reads identically to a line saying nothing happened. It uses the fixed target list now, prints the pairs the shape refused, and counts the partition in the summary.
obs The purity check refused this file on its first run over a line of PROSE describing the distance array. The check reads until the next `function` line, so a comment block belonging to the following function was attributed to the previous one. Closing a body at a column-zero comment repairs it, and the control proves that boundary from both sides by planting exactly that comment where it does damage.
obs Three of the control's plants failed on the first run and each was a real signal rather than noise: one plant was a no-op because the value it moved already equalled its replacement, one used a newline sed cannot match, and one proved a branch that had gone dead when `make_holes` left the purity list. All three were repaired rather than deleted, which is the difference between a control and a decoration.
obs The paper graded A at 90 with register at 34 percent negative sentences, four over the Field ceiling. A pass restating twenty-one sentences positively brought it to 25 percent and the grade to 92, with every number, path and stamp untouched -- a register pass changes how a finding reads and never what it says.
