recommend keep-going -- finding three is the one BAKERY can use and it has a named falsifier that costs one run: S(9,4) at 3,024 vertices, asking whether far-end-major and door-major converge as the shape grows. If they do, this is a reading about small shapes; if they do not, an allocator comparison function is worth writing into Caravan.
